60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I like Anchor! Having an engineering team actually present during the rollout sounds like they'll see the yard mess for themselves.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I strongly object to Corvus. Modular licenses are exactly how those renewal invoices started climbing. It's a trap for the budget.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Corvus is a non-starter for me too. Separate components mean separate support contracts, which leads to the finger-pointing I found in the outage reports.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Anchor sounds like the dinosaur! ""On our own servers"" means we'll just skip updates again because we're too lazy to do it!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"I worry about the ""fixed configuration"" of Meridian. Our people are already stretched; they cannot be forced into a rigid box.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, but if the engineers are here, they can help us update it! I'm worried about Tessera's ""marketplace""—that sounds like more hidden costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, you're right. A marketplace is just a fancy word for ""pay-per-feature."" Meridian's hosted suite seems more predictable for the long term.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Meridian's ""fixed configuration"" is actually a benefit. It prevents the business from drifting into chaos within months, provided the governance is tight.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"I like Tessera! It's a cloud suite, so it's always new! And a partner firm for migration means we can make them fix the data properly this time!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, governance is a shield, but it can also be a cage. I prefer Anchor. The presence of a team provides the emotional support our staff needs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm torn, but Anchor's on-site presence is the only way I trust the yard devices will actually work. I'm sticking with Anchor.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I cannot support Anchor or Tessera. The risk of ""hidden"" costs in a marketplace or on-premise maintenance is too high. Meridian is the safest financial bet.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Anchor is too risky for support ownership. On-site teams leave eventually. Meridian's regional service team and fixed process offer the accountability we lack.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"No way! Anchor is just the old way! Tessera is the future! It's fast, it's cloud, and it won't get dusty in a server room!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"We must consider the human cost. Our administrators are leaving. A partner firm like Tessera's might fill the gap, but Anchor's presence is more comforting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
